# Reminder Agent — Kiro Prompt Context

## What this project is
A smart schedule reminder agent. It lets you add tasks with a start time and duration,
automatically detects scheduling clashes, suggests conflict-free time slots, and reminds
you at the right moment so you act immediately — not just "eventually".

## Project structure
```
src/
  index.js          — CLI entry point and daemon runner
  scheduler.js      — Clash detection + auto-rescheduling logic
  reminder.js       — Reminder engine: cron jobs, urgency tiers
  storage.js        — JSON-backed task persistence layer
  task.js           — Task model and validation
  utils/
    time.js         — Time helpers (overlap check, formatting)
    notify.js       — Desktop + terminal notification wrapper
data/
  tasks.json        — Local task database (gitignored)
```

## Key behaviors
- Tasks have: title, date, startTime, duration (minutes), priority, tags
- Clash = two tasks overlap in time window (configurable MIN_GAP_MINUTES buffer)
- On clash: agent suggests the next free slot automatically
- Reminder tiers:
  1. Early warning  — REMINDER_LEAD_TIME_MINUTES before (default 15 min)
  2. Urgent         — REMINDER_URGENT_MINUTES before (default 5 min)
  3. Start now      — exactly at task time
- Daemon mode: runs as background process, polls every minute via node-cron

## Coding conventions
- ESM modules (import/export), Node 18+
- Async/await throughout, no callbacks
- Config always read from process.env (loaded via dotenv)
- All times stored as ISO 8601 strings in UTC, displayed in local timezone
- Errors are logged, never silently swallowed

## Commands
```
node src/index.js add          # interactive task creation
node src/index.js list         # show upcoming tasks
node src/index.js remove <id>  # delete a task
node src/index.js daemon       # run reminder loop in background
```
